combination of them.

3.5.2 The investigation: taking citizenship action

Taking citizenship action may be defined as a planned course of informed action to address a
citizenship issue or question of concern and aimed at delivering a benefit or change for a particular
community or wider society. Taking citizenship action in a real out-of-classroom context allows
