At this stage students should evaluate their whole investigative process and attempt to establish
what went well and what could have been done differently.

Teachers are not required to mark or assess this work but may wish to use the investigations as a
source of learning and teaching in the classroom in the form of debates, written presentations or
using e-media.

Students may wish to use the AQA Investigation template both as a record of their investigation
and as a means of recalling their work prior to the exam.

