tml","severity":"HIGH","claim":"Applying for asylum is a legal right under international law, established by the 1951 UN Refugee Convention.","truth":"Article 14 of the Universal Declaration of Human Rights recognises the right to seek and enjoy asylum. The 1951 Convention defines refugee status and provides protections, but does not expressly establish a right of asylum. Recommend a coordinated change to all repeated content, question and answer-key references rather than partial edits.","evidence":"UNHCR, Note on International Protection; UNHCR, Note on Asylum (fetched 2026-09-04)","verdict":"ADJUDICATE"},{"id":"F6","lesson":5,"field":"content_html","severity":"HIGH","claim":"member states are expected to spend at least 2% of GDP on defence","truth":"At the 2025 Hague Summit, NATO allies committed to invest 5% of GDP annually in core defence and defence- and security-related spending by 2035.","evidence":"NATO, The Hague Summit Declaration (2025); NATO, Defence investment and NATO’s 5% commitment (updated 2026) (fetched 2026-09-04)","verdict":"FIX"},{"id":"F7","lesson":5,"field":"content_html","severity":"HIGH","claim":"When the UK left the EU in January 2020 it left the EU’s institutions (the European Parliament, the European Court of Justice, the single market, the customs union).","truth":"The UK left the EU on 31 January 2020, but remained in the single market and customs union during the transition period until 31 December 2020.","evidence":"GOV.UK, Public funds: transition period guidance (fetched 2026-09-04)","verdict":"FIX"},{"id":"F8","lesson":8,"field":"content_html","severity":"HIGH","claim":"The police may stop and search only when they have reasonable grounds to suspect someone of carrying weapons, stolen goods or items for use in crime.","truth":"Reasonable grounds are usually required, but a senior officer can authorise suspicionless searches in limited circumstances, including under section 60 powers.","evidence":"GOV.UK, Police powers to stop and 