+  {"lesson":8,"field":"content_html","find":"The police may stop and search only when they have reasonable grounds to suspect someone of carrying weapons, stolen goods or items for use in crime.","replace":"Police usually need reasonable grounds to suspect someone is carrying weapons, stolen goods or items for use in crime. In limited circumstances, a senior officer can authorise searches without individual suspicion.","severity":"HIGH","note":"F8: The word ‘only’ wrongly excludes authorised no-suspicion powers."},
