+  {"lesson":12,"field":"content_html","find":"Key principles of the Geneva Conventions include: the prohibition on targeting civilians, the requirement to treat prisoners of war humanely, the protection of medical personnel and facilities, and the ban on using certain weapons such as chemical weapons and landmines.","replace":"Key rules of international humanitarian law include protecting civilians, treating prisoners of war humanely and protecting medical personnel and facilities. Separate treaties ban chemical weapons and anti-personnel landmines.","severity":"HIGH","note":"F14: The weapons bans are not provisions of the Geneva Conventions themselves."},
+  {"lesson":13,"field":"content_html","find":"To become a magistrate, a person must apply to the Judicial Appointments Commission and be assessed for qualities including good character, social awareness, sound judgement and the ability to see things from another&rsquo;s perspective.","replace":"To become a magistrate, a person applies through a local Advisory Committee on Justices of the Peace and is assessed for qualities including good character, social awareness, sound judgement and the ability to see things from another&rsquo;s perspective.","severity":"MEDIUM","note":"F15: The Judicial Appointments Commission does not recruit magistrates."}
